WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.011
Welcome to Bible and Beyond.

2
00:00:03.511 --> 00:00:07.266
A free place to read, search, and study the Bible.

3
00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:14.562
Bible and Beyond is free, non-commercial, and has no ads.

4
00:00:15.076 --> 00:00:24.067
The welcome page shows what is on the site: Bibles, classic commentaries, daily devotionals, other Christian books, and music.

5
00:00:24.575 --> 00:00:30.513
Each card has buttons to read or to search, and the menu on the left takes you to every part of the site.

6
00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.547
Let's start with the Bible reader.

7
00:00:36.074 --> 00:00:40.111
Choose a Bible, a book, and a chapter, and press Go.

8
00:00:48.269 --> 00:00:52.569
Then just keep scrolling, to read on from chapter to chapter.

9
00:00:53.092 --> 00:01:04.378
Click a verse number for more about that verse: Show in Context, Other Translations, Related Verses, the original words, the commentaries, and your own notes.

10
00:01:04.888 --> 00:01:13.217
In the Berean Standard Bible, you can also click a word, to see the Hebrew or Greek word behind it, and every verse that uses it.

11
00:01:15.967 --> 00:01:20.718
Search the Bible for words, an exact phrase, or a Strong's number.

12
00:01:21.242 --> 00:01:24.211
Here we search for, love one another.

13
00:01:31.607 --> 00:01:39.750
Every result has links: to the verse in context, the full chapter, other translations, related verses, and more.

14
00:01:40.251 --> 00:01:49.311
Search Options lets you match all the words, any word, or the exact phrase, search one Bible or several, and keep to part of the Bible.

15
00:01:49.822 --> 00:01:52.930
The results can also be filtered by book.

16
00:01:57.023 --> 00:02:04.353
Search Everything looks through the Bible, the commentaries, the devotionals, the other books, and the music, all at once.

17
00:02:08.136 --> 00:02:14.363
A search for grace finds the verses first, then what the commentators wrote, and the rest.

18
00:02:19.421 --> 00:02:29.828
The commentaries include classic works by Matthew Henry, John Gill, Adam Clarke, John Calvin, Martin Luther, Spurgeon, and more.

19
00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:33.210
Pick a book and a chapter, and press Read.

20
00:02:38.518 --> 00:02:42.017
Every Scripture reference in a note is a link to the verse.

21
00:02:50.919 --> 00:02:58.876
You can also search the commentaries, to find what the great teachers wrote about a word or a phrase, such as, born again.

22
00:03:08.218 --> 00:03:11.123
The devotionals open at today's date.

23
00:03:13.688 --> 00:03:19.417
Here is Daily Light on the Daily Path, with a reading for every morning and evening of the year.

24
00:03:22.219 --> 00:03:32.548
Other books brings classic Christian writing, from Augustine and Aquinas to Chesterton, Bunyan, Wesley, and Tozer, to read a chapter at a time.

25
00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.224
And you can search them, too.

26
00:03:47.253 --> 00:03:52.563
In the Apostles' Creed, every statement links to the Bible verse it comes from.

27
00:03:53.068 --> 00:03:55.743
Rest the pointer on one to see which.

28
00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:03.035
Christian music has hymns and songs to listen to, each with its words.

29
00:04:03.568 --> 00:04:05.558
Open a song to play it.

30
00:04:12.967 --> 00:04:17.674
And you can search the music, by title, author, or the words of a song.

31
00:04:25.386 --> 00:04:30.023
Every search page has one more choice: Search the Internet Archive.

32
00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:44.659
It searches inside millions of books and documents on archive.org, including its lending library.

33
00:04:45.168 --> 00:04:51.036
A book still under copyright can be borrowed there for an hour, free, with an Archive account.

34
00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:59.968
The FAQ answers thirty-two common questions about God, the Bible, and the Christian life.

35
00:05:00.497 --> 00:05:03.679
Choose a question, and press Show the answer.

36
00:05:05.659 --> 00:05:13.301
The answers are written by Google's Gemini A.I., with every Scripture reference as a link, and some have a note from the site owner.

37
00:05:13.838 --> 00:05:17.257
The A.I. can make mistakes, and the page says so.

38
00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:22.904
With a free account, you can do even more.

39
00:05:25.804 --> 00:05:28.237
Everything works without an account.

40
00:05:28.737 --> 00:05:34.500
A free account adds your own notes, daily devotional emails, and music playlists.

41
00:05:35.036 --> 00:05:40.857
Setting one up takes about a minute: your email address, and a password, typed twice.

42
00:05:55.751 --> 00:05:58.427
Your name and phone number are optional.

43
00:06:02.204 --> 00:06:07.909
You can write your own notes on any verse, commentary note, or devotional reading.

44
00:06:08.417 --> 00:06:12.830
Click a verse number, choose Notes, write your note, and save it.

45
00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:40.255
My Notes keeps every note in one place, with a search, and a link back to each one.

46
00:06:43.004 --> 00:06:46.259
Any devotional can be emailed to you each day.

47
00:06:46.796 --> 00:06:50.426
Choose the time and your time zone, and press the button.

48
00:06:53.168 --> 00:06:57.677
You can change the time, or stop the emails, whenever you like.

49
00:07:00.422 --> 00:07:06.658
On the music page, tick the songs you want, give the list a name, and save it as a playlist.

50
00:07:14.348 --> 00:07:18.205
Then press Play, and the songs play one after another.

51
00:07:20.938 --> 00:07:25.655
Some features are turned on for each account by the site's administrator.

52
00:07:26.155 --> 00:07:29.353
To ask for them, use the Contact page.

53
00:07:38.146 --> 00:07:45.070
With A.I. search, you describe what you are looking for in your own words, such as, comfort when someone has died.

54
00:07:48.684 --> 00:07:54.375
The A.I. suggests verses from the Bibles on the site, each with the usual links.

55
00:07:57.153 --> 00:08:06.806
In the commentaries, the other books, the music, and Search Everything, A.I. search finds passages by their meaning, even when they use other words.

56
00:08:07.307 --> 00:08:12.896
A search for, the beatitudes, finds Matthew Henry's notes on the Sermon on the Mount.

57
00:08:20.286 --> 00:08:24.296
On the FAQ page, you can also ask your own question.

58
00:08:24.796 --> 00:08:28.705
Here we ask, how can I pray when I don't know what to say?

59
00:08:29.205 --> 00:08:33.088
The answer comes back with every Scripture reference as a link.

60
00:08:43.739 --> 00:08:47.778
Conversations is a place for members to share with one another.

61
00:08:48.289 --> 00:08:53.013
Read what others have written, reply to them, and write posts of your own.

62
00:09:04.272 --> 00:09:09.444
You can search every post and reply, and only you can change or delete your own.

63
00:09:13.739 --> 00:09:19.362
And whenever you need it, the Help page is a full user guide, with pictures of every feature.

64
00:09:21.584 --> 00:09:23.928
This video is there, too.

65
00:09:27.553 --> 00:09:31.979
Try Bible and Beyond today, at bible and beyond dot com.

66
00:09:32.479 --> 00:09:36.246
It's free, with no ads, and nothing to install.
